A script gets onto the VM without a run that does the lowering itself ([measured here](docs/ENGINES-FIRST-RUNS-2026-11-25.md)). Its first run takes {{ratio.hello.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}} of the tree-walker's time on `hello` and {{ratio.lines-500.cig-auto-cold.cig-tree}} on a 500-line script. Its second, which starts the lowering in a process of its own, takes {{ratio.hello.cig-auto-second.cig-tree}} and {{ratio.lines-500.cig-auto-second.cig-tree}} ({{earlier:start-one-cpu:ratio.hello.cig-auto-second.cig-tree}} and {{earlier:start-one-cpu:ratio.lines-500.cig-auto-second.cig-tree}} where that process has to share one CPU with it). From its third run on, cigo's 20,992-line script starts in {{median.orchestrate.cig-auto}} ms where the tree-walker takes {{median.orchestrate.cig-tree}}, and the 500-line script in {{median.lines-500.cig-auto}} ms against {{median.lines-500.cig-tree}}.
